{"id": "Dev4Mxhx84f", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Why does Maa Lakshmi ride an OWL? 🦉 This Diwali, her owl went ON STRIKE for a Diwali bonus 😂 (Vahana Union, Part 2!)\n\nEvery day of Diwali has a story, and somebody has to carry the gods:\n\n🪔 Day 1, Dhanteras: at dusk a lamp is lit for Yama, facing south (Yama Deepdaan). His ride? A buffalo.\n🪔 Day 2, Choti Diwali: Krishna and Satyabhama flew on Garuda to defeat Narakasura (Bhagavata Purana 10.59).\n🪔 Day 3, Lakshmi Puja: on Amavasya, the darkest night of the month, Maa Lakshmi comes on her owl, and Ganesha on his mouse.\n🪔 Day 4, Govardhan Puja: Krishna asked Vraja to worship the hill and the COWS (Bhagavata Purana 10.24).\n🪔 Day 5, Bhai Dooj: Yama visits his sister Yamuna, who feeds him at her home.\n\nSo yes, the owl brings Maa Lakshmi on the darkest night… and then gets called \"ullu\" for the other 364 days 😅\n\nThis Diwali, gift a story 📚 Rishi Katha Books 1–3 (Shailputri, Brahmacharini, Chandraghanta) are picture books for kids: set of 3 for ₹500 at rishikatha.com (link in bio).\n\nSave this for the 5 days of Diwali and send it to the ULLU of your house 🦉\nIs your name LAKSHMI, SHREE, KAMALA or PADMA? Comment it! 👇\n\n#diwali #diwali2026 #maalakshmi #lakshmipuja #dhanteras #narakchaturdashi #govardhanpuja #bhaidooj #ganesha #owl #indianmythology #hindumythology #kidsbooks #funnyreels #rishikatha", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1792568028, "like_count": 5616, "comment_count": 30, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-39319971584317347a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 47.004, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr22-1.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQNcLL07dSmhxGEFxa8HA5AZwwMkXleDongvNwhYQa-BTvDoE9q2SRWjsBFdq66nftW3PFI3uod_Aq52eDBIFGr7LkHDu-FsMEyJRhA.mp4?_nc_cat=106&_nc_oc=AdprURF